// Let the terminal stop and start fldigi.
//
// WSPR needs the USB codec and the codec is exclusive: `arecord -l` reports
// `Subdevices: 0/1` while fldigi holds it and every capture fails with
// "audio open error: Device or resource busy". There is no `dmix`/`dsnoop`
// to share through on this board. So WSPR stops `cyberdeck-fldigi` for the
// duration of a session and starts it again afterwards.
//
// **Not through sudo.** A sudoers rule for the same two commands works from
// a login shell and fails from inside `cyberdeck-ui.service`, which has no
// tty and no PAM session and whose `CapabilityBoundingSet` is narrowed to
// CAP_SYS_TTY_CONFIG — so the setuid helper cannot hold the capabilities it
// expects after becoming root. Verified on the deck: `sudo -u deck sudo -n
// systemctl stop cyberdeck-fldigi` succeeds at a prompt while the same call
// from the service does not.
//
// This is the same failure the WiFi screen hit, for the same reason, and the
// comment in 10-cyberdeck-networkmanager.rules states it in full: a systemd
// service has no seat and no session, polkit sees a subject that is neither
// active nor inactive, and the call falls through to auth_admin with no
// agent to ask.
//
// Scoped as narrowly as that one:
//
//   * one user, not a group. DECK_USER is substituted at build time.
//   * one action id, `manage-units`, not the org.freedesktop.systemd1 prefix.
//   * ONE UNIT. `action.lookup("unit")` is checked against
//     cyberdeck-fldigi.service, so this grants nothing over any other unit
//     on the board — notably not over cyberdeck-ui itself, which would let
//     the terminal restart or stop the thing asking.
//   * three verbs. Stop and start are what WSPR uses; restart is included
//     because a failed restore is otherwise unrecoverable from the panel.
//
// Install: /etc/polkit-1/rules.d/10-cyberdeck-services.rules, root-owned,
// mode 644. See docs/wspr_deploy.md section 4b.

polkit.addRule(function (action, subject) {
    if (action.id !== "org.freedesktop.systemd1.manage-units") {
        return;
    }
    if (subject.user !== "@DECK_USER@") {
        return;
    }
    var unit = action.lookup("unit");
    var verb = action.lookup("verb");
    var verbs = ["stop", "start", "restart"];
    if (unit === "cyberdeck-fldigi.service" && verbs.indexOf(verb) !== -1) {
        return polkit.Result.YES;
    }
});
